# The previous contents set CXX11, CXX11STD and CXX11FLAGS. Those variables have no effect on
# modern R (which selects the standard via CXX_STD), so the file was inert while still being the
# kind of compiler-variable override R CMD check flags. It is replaced with the portable OpenMP
# idiom.
#
# $(SHLIB_OPENMP_CXXFLAGS) expands to whatever the platform's toolchain needs, and to nothing at all
# where OpenMP is unavailable -- notably stock Apple clang. That is the intended behaviour: the
# package then builds single-threaded rather than failing to build, and the parallel regions are
# guarded by #ifdef _OPENMP. moran_max_threads() reports which case applies, so a benchmark can
# never claim a threaded timing on a serial build.

PKG_CXXFLAGS = $(SHLIB_OPENMP_CXXFLAGS)
PKG_LIBS = $(SHLIB_OPENMP_CXXFLAGS)
